{"id": "EUVD-2026-105094", "enisaUuid": "09e8a000-5e80-30d8-86d1-28ab60e5f57d", "description": "Froxlor before 2.3.15 contains a symlink following vulnerability in Statistics::makeChownWithNewStats that allows authenticated customers to take ownership of arbitrary host directories by abusing the root-run traffic cron. Attackers can replace the goaccess statistics directory in their document root with a symlink, causing chown -R to hand root-owned trees to them and enabling root escalation.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T01:47:53", "baseScore": 9.4, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:H/SI:H/SA:H", "references": ["https://github.com/froxlor/froxlor/security/advisories/GHSA-vwjv-x8ff-4cvv", "https://github.com/froxlor/froxlor/commit/0805a7e16a223d528b51d8cacfaff54217b9d8f8", "https://github.com/froxlor/froxlor/releases/tag/2.3.15", "https://github.com/froxlor/froxlor/blob/2.3.14/lib/Froxlor/Http/Statistics.php#L144-L162", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/froxlor-before-2.3.15-symlink-following-privilege-escalation-via-traffic-cron"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j3hm-8rm8-m243", "CVE-2026-113678"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d07e3fce-009f-3edb-8a5b-bd8a9498b967", "product": {"name": "Froxlor", "vendor": {"name": "froxlor"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.3.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a6d57e34-00bf-3405-9295-534a87d56b91", "vendor": {"name": "froxlor"}}], "isExploited": false}